  - A clip with no words is listed with why.
- **Head of the phase:** TX-S1 runs and its verdict is recorded; then TX-10…TX-14 are recorded.
- **Core.** `plan.rs`'s `audio_segment` writes `path` and `origin` on an audio segment whose voice
  is inside a nest, from the voice's stages (TX-10), and nothing on any other segment. New test
  `core/tests/plan_instances.rs`: a plan with no nest is byte-identical to `d0661e5d`'s on the
  existing fixtures; a nest shown by two clips gives two segments with distinct `path`s and the
  right `origin`s; a nest inside a nest gives a three-id path. No op, no format change.
- **FFI:** none (the plan is `rc_composition_plan`'s).
- **Swift.**
  - New, pure, with no AppKit:
    - `TimelineTranscript.swift`: the model, its tokens, TX-10's order, heard rule and identity;
    - `TimelineTranscript+Rules.swift`: nested placement, TX-11's reasons, the same speech
      twice.
  - New, the rest:
    - `TranscriptFill.swift`: one per document; its owners (TX-12), a serial queue off main, the
      `CancelToken`, progress and `DeviceTranscriptCache.store`;
    - `AgentServer+TimelineTranscript.swift`: the tool;
    - `AgentCatalog+Transcript.swift`: its entry, in a new file because `AgentCatalog+Clips.swift`
      is 574 lines.
  - Changed:
    - `CompositionPlan.swift`: `PlanSegment` decodes `path` (default the clip alone) and
      `origin` (default nil), leniently as its other keys;
    - `AgentServer+CreatorJobs.swift` (CJ0's T8): the tool's row in `creatorHandlers`, and its
      name in the road map's off-main set. If T8 landed without such a set, TX1 adds
      `creatorOffMainTools` there and its one `.union` line to `offMainTools`
      (`AgentServer.swift:115`), wiring in a frozen file;
    - `SilenceDetector.swift`: `isAudible` widened from private to internal, a visibility change
      with no move;
    - `DeviceTranscriptCache.swift`: its doc's reader list;
    - `AssistantPrompt.swift`: `get_timeline_transcript` joins the captions topic's TOOL list.
      The row's words do not change, so the guide stays 1,498 characters (F4, F6);
    - `SpeechEngine.swift`, only on TX-S1's playback condition: its toll first, then a priority
      argument on `transcribe`.
- **MCP mirror:** `get_timeline_transcript` (TX-13), app-state and off main. Product tools go to
  107.
- **Docs.**
  - `docs/guide/cleanup-tools.md`: "Reading a clip's transcript" gains the timeline read, its
    paging and the fill's cost.
  - Spec: a new `07.9f-agent-transcript.md` and its README row; §7.2 (the nested audio segment's
    `path` and `origin`); §5.6's `device-transcripts` paragraph (its readers, the whole-file
    run).
  - §11: TX-10…TX-14, and TR-14's Amended line.
  - Map entries the orchestrator applies: `app/CLAUDE.md` (`TimelineTranscript.swift`,
    `+Rules`, `TranscriptFill.swift`, `AgentServer+TimelineTranscript.swift`,
    `AgentCatalog+Transcript.swift`; `CompositionPlan.swift`'s new keys); `core/CLAUDE.md`
    (`plan.rs`'s nested keys); root `CLAUDE.md`'s app-state tool list (`get_timeline_transcript`)
    and its product tool count.
- **Acceptance:** the read over each fixture equals the probe's expected tokens. A second read
  recognises nothing. Stop leaves nothing stored. Every plan without a nest is byte-identical.
- **Proof** (`timeline_transcript_probe.swift`, `timeline_transcript_proof.py`, run whole once
  against Release):
  - P1 two tracks and three media read back in TX-10's order, ties by track;
  - P2 a muted clip's words absent and its unmuted twin's present;
  - P3 a nest's words at the nest clip's start plus their inner time, not editable with TX-11's
    sentence;
  - P3b a nest shown by two clips: its words twice, at each clip's times, with distinct
    identities;
  - P3c a nest clip trimmed shorter than its nest: only the words it plays, none past its end;
  - P3d a duplicated clip: its words twice, k 0 then 1, and a selection of the second survives a
    ripple before both;
  - P3e a nested clip with its audio switched off: under `no_words`, named with its nest;
  - P4 a transition's words not editable;
  - P5 a locked track's words not editable;
  - P6 a ramped clip's words equal `get_transcript`'s for that clip, word for word;
  - P7 a reversed clip under `no_words` with the gate's sentence;
  - P8 the same-speech note on a duplicated `say` track;
  - P9 an `assemblyai_fake` cache read first, engine `assemblyai`, with `media[]` carrying
    `fillers_reported`;
  - P10 one stored run per media covering the whole file, read back from
    `cache/device-transcripts/`;
  - P11 a second call answers with no recognition;
  - P11b a clip trimmed 3 s outward, then a second clip of the same file placed: no recognition
    runs;
  - P12 Stop answers "The transcription was cancelled." and stores nothing;
  - P12b two wants: a tool call's Stop while the tab shows leaves the fill running, and it lands;
  - P13 paging at 2,000 words;
  - G rows: each refusal's sentence.
  - `transcript_proof.py` reruns as a regression, since its cache file is shared.
- **Mutants** (8): the heard test dropped; tie order by track reversed; the nest offset lost;
  `path` written on a top-level segment (the byte-identity test); k left out of the identity;
  the fill read over the played span instead of the whole file (P11b); a Stop cancelling every
  want; the page boundary off by one.
- **Manual checks:** none. Nothing here is for a person to judge.
- **Depends on:** CJ0 (T1, T5, T8, T9), with TX-S1 run and TX-10…TX-14 recorded at the head.

